/* Keren Vav often has different crediting rates between the base savings and additional
savings.  On
the active portion of the policy, we model the two parts separately and can apply
different rates.
However, we do not separate in the PUP portion.  Therefore we need to derive an
appropriate weighted
crediting rate based on the relative proportions at the point of PUP, how we would have
expected them
to grow until maturity, and the existing PUP crediting rate.
When running with a distribution we have various maturity ages.  However, for simplicity
here, we assume
a fixed (data) maturity age in the calculation of the weighted crediting rate, and hold
the rate constant
after the data maturity point.  */
double years_to_mat = (maturity_period_w - t + 1.0) / pv_period_im;
if (years_to_mat < SMALL_DOUBLE)  // i.e. we are in a distribution run and past the data
maturity age
