but we do take into account indexation on the mishtatef policies. */
/* The actual annuity cashflow (gimla_post_maturity) will be based on this column, so we need to
calculate
the indexed value of the average payment in the period.  As annuity payments are made at the end
of the month,
this will come out slightly later than the middle of the period.  For example, if running the
model quarterly,
then the average payment is 2/3rds of the way through.  The formulae here reflect this. */
if (t <= maturity_period_sub || t > model_end_period)
return NO_AVG;
// For non-participating funds, the payment is fixed.
if (prod_fund_group_post <= 7)
return monthly_payment_internal_e(t-1);
