We reserve for the standard joint-life mekadem for the maslul when life 1 is still alive.
We reserve for a single-life mekadem when life 1 is dead and life 2 still alive, taking into
account
the survivor percentage.
Technically if life 2 is dead we should reserve for a single-life mekadem, but in practice we are
not informed and so continue to reserve for the higher joint-life amount.
*/
double FAO_life2 = fao_sl0_sex2_tables_post_attime(per+1) / 100.0
* gimla_feff_antisel_postret;
return monthly_payment_internal_e(per) / gimla_antisel_ratio
* ((gimla_if_life1andlife2_b(per+1) + gimla_if_life1_notlife2_b(per+1))
* ann_conv_fac_feff(per+1) / 100.0 * gimla_feff_antisel_postret
+ gimla_if_notlife1_life2_b(per+1) * FAO_life2 * survivor_pc);
